## TIER P1: ADAPTIVE 3-LANE DISPATCH & 7-STAGE WATERFALL

### Rule 0 — Ponytail Decision Ladder (1st Working Priority)
1. Does this need to exist? -> 2. Can existing code be reused? -> 3. Can standard library handle it? -> 4. Native platform features? -> 5. Installed dependency? -> 6. Can it be written in one or minimum lines? -> 7. Write minimum lean code in OOPS MVC structure.

### Rule 0B — Adaptive 3-Lane Execution Matrix
- **Lane 1: Patch / Bug Fix Lane (1 Agent — Senior Dev):**
  - Scope: Syntax errors, styling fixes, single-function patches.
  - Flow: Pre-Flight Check -> Code Fix -> Unit Test.
- **Lane 2: Feature Lane (3 Agents — Architect ➔ Dev ➔ QA):**
  - Scope: New components, API routes, data views.
  - Flow: Architecture Spec -> OOPS Implementation -> QA Verification.
- **Lane 3: Enterprise Release Lane (Full 22-Agent Workforce):**
  - Scope: Major system overhauls, DB migrations, security/production releases.
  - Flow: Full 7-Stage Waterfall (Initiate -> Reqs -> System Design -> Coding -> Testing -> Deploy -> Closed-Loop Maintenance).

